licant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOTO LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAYUMI YOSHITAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA YASUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAEKI YOSHIMITSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAYUMI, YOSHITAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAEKI, YOSHIMITSU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method capable of efficiently producing a high-performance material having a high-performance photocatalytic function and a device for the method. A photocatalytic coating composition containing a photocatalytic metal oxide and/or its precursor is applied onto the surface of a base material and the surface of the base material is then quickly heated to fix the photocatalytic metal oxide on the surface. This quick heating makes it possible to efficiently produce a high-performance material having a high-performance photocatalytic function. A device capable of performing this quick heating continuously immediately after the production of the base material can efficiently produce a high-performance material having a photocatalytic function.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de produire efficacement un matériau performant, à fonction photocatalytique haute performance, ainsi qu'un dispositif utilisé pour ce procédé. Une composition de revêtement photocatalytique contenant un oxyde métallique photocatalytique et/ou son précurseur est appliquée sur la surface d'un matériau de base, après quoi la surface est chauffée rapidement en vue de fixer l'oxyde métallique photocatalytique sur cette surface. Ce chauffage rapide permet de produire efficacement un matériau performant à fonction photocatalytique haute performance. Un dispositif capable d'effectuer ce chauffage rapide, en continu, immédiatement après la production du matériau de base, peut produire efficacement un tel matériau haute performance à fonction photocatalytique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>